# --- Raft's finds in the shallows round the island and over the bay (lib_sea) ---------------------------------------------
call shallows r=165 deep=5 n=2

# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (24 steps, 4 chapters) =============================================
info title=Heart of Fire
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Two great peaks over a burnt bay: the Ember, a live volcano with a fire-bird in its crater, and the Green Mother, sleeping, her heart stolen. The island is ash; its people left in their canoes. Find the three shards of the Bloomstone, mend it, carry it past the Cinderwraith - and give the Mother back her heart.
island on.arrive=message||Grey ash where a jungle should be, dead trees on the slopes of two huge peaks, a burnt village by the bay. Over the western peak, something circles in the smoke.

story prybar|Pry bar|quest:Vasagatan_Crowbar|The canoe builders' pry bar from the canoe house.
story shard|Shard of the Bloomstone|Placeable_Utopia_LightBottleYellow|A shard of green stone with the sun caught in it - a third of the Green Mother's heart.
story livecoal|Live coal|Placeable_Lantern_FireBasket|A coal from the lava tubes' glow, still burning in its clay pot.
story bloomstone|The Bloomstone|Placeable_Utopia_LightBottleWhite|The Green Mother's heart, whole again: green as a leaf, warm as skin.
story seedpod|The Mother's seed pod|Seed_Palm|A seed pod left on the shrine where the Bloomstone was laid: the island's first fruit.

note eldercarving The elders' carving | (carved round the great post)\n\nWhen the island was young the Green Mother slept on the eastern peak and the Ember slept on the western one. In the Mother's shrine lay the Bloomstone, her heart, and while it lay there the island was green.\n\nA navigator came, Corvan, who wanted a ship that never lacked a wind. He took the Bloomstone.\n\nThe Ember woke. Fire came down the mountain and the green went grey, and the Cinderwraith rose out of the Ember's mouth and has not slept since. Corvan's ship burned in the bay as he ran.\n\nWe took the canoes and went over the sea. If the Bloomstone ever comes home to the Mother, we will come home too.
note navlog Navigator's log | CORVAN LISLE - LOG\n\nI have it. The Bloomstone, green as a leaf with the sun in it. Already the sails fill with no wind.\n\n...\n\nThe mountain is burning. The bird of fire is over the bay. The stone CRACKED in my hands when the mast came down - three pieces. One is in the hold with me; the hatch is jammed. The bird took one in its claws and dropped it in its black temple on the burning mountain's shoulder. The third fell into the river of fire, and the beetles dragged it into the tubes.\n\nIf anyone reads this: put it back. Put it back.
note templecarving The temple's carving | (cut into the black stone over the braziers)\n\nLight the three fires as the sun lights them -\ndawn, noon, dusk:\nthe east, the high one, the west -\nand the stone door will open.
note mothersong The Mother's song | (carved on a stone by the dry basin)\n\nThree that were one, lay them in my bowl.\nCarry my heart over the saddle where the Ember watches.\nLay it on my stone at the top of the world,\nand I will wake.
note welcomepost The elders' welcome | (freshly carved, the wood still pale)\n\nThe Mother is awake and the island is green. We came home on the morning tide and found her heart in the shrine and the Ember asleep.\n\nWhoever you are - you are one of us now. Our gift is in the canoe house.
note canoebox Canoe house box | The canoe builders' box: adzes, cord - and a long iron pry bar, for planks that won't come apart.
loot canoebox story:prybar*1;Rope*3
prop canoebox loot.refill=0
note wreckhold Navigator's hold | Corvan's hold, its hatch pried open: charred cargo, salt-stiff charts - and in a box lined with moss, the first shard of the Bloomstone.
loot wreckhold story:shard*1;Scrap*3;TitaniumOre*1
prop wreckhold loot.refill=0
prop wreckhold if.open=has|story:prybar|1
prop wreckhold else.open=message||The hold's hatch is jammed shut with fire-warped planks. A pry bar would do it.
note tubechest Tubes' chamber chest | A beetle-gnawed box in the glowing chamber at the tubes' end: the second shard, warm to the touch.
loot tubechest story:shard*1;CopperOre*2
prop tubechest loot.refill=0
note emberpot Ember pot | A clay pot in the lava's glow, a coal burning in it that never goes out.
loot emberpot story:livecoal*1;Clay*2
prop emberpot loot.refill=0
note sanctumchest Sanctum chest | In the black sanctum, where the Cinderwraith dropped it: the third shard of the Bloomstone.
loot sanctumchest story:shard*1;TradeToken*3
prop sanctumchest loot.refill=0
note eldersgift Elders' gift | The elders' gift, in the canoe house: seeds of every tree that grows here, the gardeners' plans for terraced beds, a water gourd that never turns sour - and titanium and coin from Corvan's ship, which the sea gave back.
loot eldersgift Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3*1;Blueprint_Cropplot_Medium_Tier3*1;Blueprint_Canteen*1;Seed_Mango*4;Seed_Banana*4;Seed_Palm*4;TitaniumIngot*4;TradeToken*12
prop eldersgift loot.refill=0
prop eldersgift if.open=signal|bloomed
prop eldersgift else.open=message||A chest bound with green cord, a carved leaf on its lid. It is not yours yet.
note villagestore Village store box | The village store's box, half burnt: rope, stone tools, dried fish.
loot villagestore Rope*3;Stone*4;Cooked_Herring*2
prop villagestore loot.refill=0
note fishbox Fishers' box | The fishers' box: hooks, line, a net with holes burnt in it.
loot fishbox FishingBait_Simple*3;Rope*2;Plank*4
prop fishbox loot.refill=0
note beachbarrel Beached barrel | A barrel from Corvan's ship, washed up on the black sand.
loot beachbarrel Plank*6;Nail*8;Scrap*2
prop beachbarrel loot.refill=0
note wreckbarrel Wreck's galley barrel | The ship's galley barrel: salt pork gone to leather, and scrap.
loot wreckbarrel Scrap*4;MetalOre*2;Leather*1
prop wreckbarrel loot.refill=0
note tubecache Side tunnel cache | A cache in a side tunnel: someone's lamp, and ore they never carried out.
loot tubecache MetalOre*3;CopperOre*2;BioFuel*1
prop tubecache loot.refill=0
note templeoffering Temple offering box | An offering box in the temple: black glass, gold, and a bundle of feathers.
loot templeoffering TradeToken*4;Feather*4;Glass*2
prop templeoffering loot.refill=0
note springbox Box by the basin | A box by the dry basin: a gardener's trowel, seed jars, sealed.
loot springbox Seed_Banana*2;Seed_Pineapple*2;Clay*3
prop springbox loot.refill=0
note cairnbox Cairn box | A box in the cairn on the pass: what travellers left for travellers.
loot cairnbox HealingSalve*2;PlasticBottle_Water*2;Rope*2
prop cairnbox loot.refill=0

prop brazier1 obj.name=brazier1
prop brazier1 beh.use=Light the eastern brazier (dawn)
prop brazier1 if.use=has|story:livecoal|1
prop brazier1 on.use=message||The coal catches the oil on the eastern stand. Dawn.\nshow|flame1\nsignal||br1\nsound||event:/crafting/torch
prop brazier1 else.use=message||A cold brazier stand. You'd need fire - the Ember's own, from the tubes.
prop brazier2 obj.name=brazier2
prop brazier2 beh.use=Light the high brazier (noon)
prop brazier2 if.use=has|story:livecoal|1\nsignal|br1
prop brazier2 on.use=message||The high brazier blazes. Noon.\nshow|flame2\nsignal||br2\nsound||event:/crafting/torch
prop brazier2 else.use=message||It won't catch. "As the sun lights them: dawn, noon, dusk."
prop brazier3 obj.name=brazier3
prop brazier3 beh.use=Light the western brazier (dusk)
prop brazier3 if.use=has|story:livecoal|1\nsignal|br2
prop brazier3 on.use=message||The western brazier flares. Dusk - and with a grinding the stone door of the sanctum sinks into the ground.\nshow|flame3\nopen|sanctumdoor\nsound||event:/exploring/temperence/selene/gate_open
prop brazier3 else.use=message||It won't catch. "As the sun lights them: dawn, noon, dusk."
